{
  "title": "Writing of Will before death",
  "data": "The Holy Prophet (s) is reported to have said, \"Whoever fails to write his will sensibly before his death lacks reason and manliness.\" He (s) was asked, \"How should the excellent writing of one's will be, O Messenger of Allah?\" He (s) instructed: in the last hours of his lifetime, when people gather around him, he must say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاطِرَ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ عَالِمَ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الرَّحْمٰنَ الرَّحِيْمَ اِنِّىْۤ اَعْهَدُ اِلَيْكَ اَنِّىْۤ اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَاَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA FAATIRAS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI A'AALIMAL GHAYBI WASH SHAHAADATIR RAHMAANAR RAHEEM, INNEE A'-HADU ILAYKA INNEE ASH-HADU AL LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU WA ANNA MUHAMMADAN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHI A'BDUHU WA RASOOLUH\nO Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful: verily I make this covenant with You, that I bear witness there is no god except Allah, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad, Allah's blessings be upon him and his Household, is His servant and His messenger,\nوَاَنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْعَثُ مَنْ فِى الْقُبُوْرِ وَاَنَّ الْحِسَابَ حَقٌّ وَاَنَّ الْجَنَّةَ حَقٌّ وَاَنَّ مَا وُعِدَ فِيْهَا مِنَ النَّعِيْمِ مِنَ الْمَاْكَلِ وَالْمَشْرَبِ وَالنِّكَاحِ حَقٌّ وَاَنَّ النَّارَ حَقٌّ وَاَنَّ الْاِيْمَانَ حَقٌّ وَاَنَّ الدِّيْنَ كَمَا وَصَفَ وَاَنَّ الْاِسْلَامَ كَمَا شَرَعَ وَاَنَّ الْقَوْلَ كَمَا قَالَ وَاَنَّ الْقُرْاٰنَ كَمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ الْمُبِيْنُ\nWA ANNAS SAA-A'TA AATIYATUL LAA RAYBA FEEHAA WA ANNALLAAHA YAB-A'THU MAN FIL QUBOOR, WA ANNAL HISAABA HAQQ, WA ANNAL JANNATA HAQQ, WA ANNA MAA WU-I'DA FEEHAA MINAN NA-E'EMI MINAL MA-KALI WAL MASHRABI WAN NIKAAHI HAQQ, WA ANNAN NAARA HAQQ, WA ANNAL EEMAANA HAQQ, WA ANNAD DEENA KAMAA WASAF, WA ANNAL ISLAAMA KAMAA SHARA-A', WA ANNAL QAWLA KAMAA QAAL, WA ANNAL QUR-AANA KAMAA ANZAL, WA ANNALLAAHA HUWAL HAQQUL MUBEEN\nand that the Hour is coming, no doubt about it, and that Allah will raise up whoever is in the graves, and that the Reckoning is true, and Paradise is true, and what is promised therein of bliss — of food, drink, and marriage — is true, and the Fire is true, and faith is true, and the religion is as He has described, and Islam is as He has legislated, and the word is as He has said, and the Qur'an is as He has revealed, and that Allah is the manifest Truth,\nوَاَنِّىْۤ اَعْهَدُ اِلَيْكَ فِىْ دَارِ الدُّنْيَا اَنِّىْ رَضِيْتُ بِكَ رَبًّا وَبِالْاِسْلَامِ دِيْنًا وَبِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ نَبِيًّا وَبِعَلِيٍّ وَلِيًّا وَبِالْقُرْاٰنِ كِتَابًا وَاَنَّ اَهْلَ بَيْتِ نَبِيِّكَ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ اَئِمَّتِىْ\nWA ANNEE A'-HADU ILAYKA FEE DAARID DUNYAAA INNEE RADEETU BIKA RABBAW WA BIL ISLAAMI DEENAW WA BI-MUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHI NABIYYAW WA BI-A'LIYYIW WALIYYAW WA BIL QUR-AANI KITAABAW WA ANNA AHLA BAYTI NABIYYIKA A'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAMU A-IMMATEE\nand that I make this further covenant with You in the abode of this world, that I am content with You as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, with Muhammad — Allah's blessings be upon him and his Household — as my prophet, with Ali as my guardian, with the Qur'an as my book, and that the Household of Your Prophet, peace be upon him and upon them, are my Imams,\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ ثِقَتِىْ عِنْدَ شِدَّتِىْ وَرَجَاۤئِىْ عِنْدَ كُرْبَتِىْ وَعُدَّتِىْ عِنْدَ الْاُمُوْرِ الَّتِىْ تَنْزِلُ بِىْ وَاَنْتَ وَلِيِّىْ فِىْ نِعْمَتِىْ وَاِلٰهِىْ وَاِلٰهُ اٰبَاۤئِىْ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ وَلَا تَكِلْنِىْ اِلٰى نَفْسِىْ طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ اَبَدًا وَاٰنِسْ فِىْ قَبْرِىْ وَحْشَتِىْ وَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ عِنْدَكَ عَهْدًا يَّوْمَ اَلْقَاكَ مَنْشُوْرًا\nALLAAHUMMA ANTA THIQATEE I'NDA SHIDDATEE WA RAJAAA-EE I'NDA KURBATEE WA U'DDATEE I'NDAL UMOORIL LATEE TANZILU BEE, WA ANTA WALIYYEE FEE NI'MATEE WA ILAAHEE WA ILAAHU AABAAA-EE, SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHI WA LAA TAKILNEE ILAA NAFSEE TARFATA A'YNIN ABADAA, WA AANIS FEE QABREE WAHSHATEE WAJ-A'L LEE I'NDAKA A'HDAY YAWMA ALQAAKA MANSHOORAA\nO Allah, You are my trust in my hardship, my hope in my distress, and my resort in the affairs that befall me; and You are my guardian in my blessing, and my God and the God of my forefathers. Send blessings upon Muhammad and his Household, and do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, ever; and ease my sense of isolation in my grave, and grant me with You a covenant on the day I meet You, unfolded.\nThe Holy Prophet (s) then added, \"This is the covenant of the moribund when he makes his will, which is obligatory upon each Muslim individual.\"\nCommenting on this, Imam al-Sadiq (a) is reported to have said: certifying this fact, Allah the All-blessed and All-exalted says in Surah Maryam: \"They shall not control intercession, save he who has made a covenant with the All-beneficent.\"\nThe Holy Prophet (s) then instructed Imam Ali (a) to learn this covenant and advise the members of his household and his adherents (i.e. the Shi'ah) to learn it. He (s) added, \"I have been taught this by Archangel Gabriel.\""
}
